{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "d73c1700-6d8b-5e84-93e3-e4d60c17518d",
  "Description": "Bouncing balls; every impact flashes at the point where it happens.\n\nThe Contacts output of [PhysicsWorld] holds one point per impact of the current frame, with the impact speed in F1. Here a second [DrawMeshAtPoints] draws a bright sphere at each of them, so an impact shows as a one-frame flash.\n\nAKA: collision events, impacts, hits, sparks, contact points\n\nTips\n- Contacts last one frame: feed them to a particle emitter for sparks or dust that linger.\n- Raise ContactSpeed on [PhysicsWorld] to report hard hits only.\n- Unused points of the buffer have zero scale, so they draw nothing.",
